Passage: REG, Annex III

[0] ANNEX III ESSENTIAL HEALTH AND SAFETY REQUIREMENTS RELATING TO THE DESIGN AND CONSTRUCTION OF MACHINERY OR RELATED PRODUCTS PART A Definitions For the purposes of this Annex, the following definitions apply:
[1] (a) ‘hazard’ means a potential source of injury or damage to health;
[2] (b) ‘danger zone’ means any zone within and/or around machinery or a related product in which a person is subject to a risk to his or her health or safety;
[3] (c) ‘exposed person’ means any person wholly or partially in a danger zone;
[4] (d) ‘operator’ means the person or persons installing, operating, adjusting, maintaining, cleaning, repairing or moving machinery or a related product;
[5] (e) ‘risk’ means a combination of the probability and the degree of an injury or damage to health that can arise in a hazardous situation;
[6] (f) ‘guard’ means a part of machinery or a related product used specifically to provide protection by means of a physical barrier;
[7] (g) ‘protective device’ means a device (other than a guard) which reduces the risk, either alone or in conjunction with a guard;
[8] (h) ‘intended use’ means the use of machinery or a related product in accordance with the information provided in the instructions for use;
[9] (i) ‘reasonably foreseeable misuse’ means the use of machinery or a related product in a way not intended in the instructions for use, but which may result from readily predictable human behaviour.
[10] PART B General principles 1.
[11] By the iterative process of risk assessment and risk reduction referred to in the first subparagraph, the manufacturer shall:
[12] (a) determine the limits of the machinery or related product, which include the intended use and any reasonably foreseeable misuse thereof;
[13] (b) identify the hazards that may be generated by the machinery or related product and the associated hazardous situations;
[14] (c) estimate the risks, taking into account the severity of the possible injury or damage to health and the probability of its occurrence;
[15] (d) evaluate the risks, with a view to determining whether risk reduction is required, in accordance with the objective of this Regulation;
[16] (e) eliminate the hazards or reduce the risks associated with these hazards by application of protective measures, in the order of priority established in section 1.1.2(b).
[17] The risk assessment and risk reduction shall include hazards that might arise during the lifecycle of the machinery or related product that are foreseeable at the time of placing the machinery or related product on the market as an intended evolution of its fully or partially self-evolving behaviour or logic as a result of the machinery or related product designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy.
[18] The risk assessment and risk reduction shall include risks resulting from interactions between machinery in order to achieve the same end that are arranged and controlled so that they function as an integral whole, thus forming machinery as defined in Article 3, point 1, point (d).
